### FFmpeg — GNU Lesser General Public License v3 (dynamically linked)

  FFmpeg
  Copyright (c) 2000-2026 the FFmpeg developers
  https://ffmpeg.org/

daw_01 decodes and encodes video through the FFmpeg libraries (libavcodec,
libavformat, libavutil, libswscale, libswresample) via the rsmpeg / rusty_ffmpeg
crates.  The libraries are **dynamically linked** as unmodified shared objects
and are **not part of this repository** (third_party/ffmpeg is gitignored and
fetched per machine by `make fetch-ffmpeg`).

The build used is BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds `n7.1 win64-lgpl-shared`, configured
without `--enable-gpl` and without `--enable-nonfree`, and with
`--enable-version3`.  All GPL-only external libraries are disabled in that
configuration (`--disable-libx264 --disable-libx265 --disable-libxavs2
--disable-libxvid --disable-librubberband --disable-libvidstab --disable-frei0r
--disable-avisynth`).  `--enable-version3` upgrades FFmpeg from LGPL v2.1+ to
**LGPL v3**, which is compatible with the GPL v3 this program is licensed under.
The exact configure line of the build in use is printed by
`third_party/ffmpeg/bin/ffmpeg.exe -version`, and is shown inside daw_01 under
**Help > About**, read back from the running library rather than hard-coded.

The exact build daw_01 pins is:

  ffmpeg-n7.1.5-16-g9a4bb2c579-win64-lgpl-shared-7.1.zip
  sha256 a950596cea0bf9766f169dae6f1e6eb623aa1ccfd2822cd20cd2874b120d4086
  FFmpeg source: FFmpeg/FFmpeg commit 9a4bb2c579a16b0469759743d6917d9e8e3cb8c6
  Build recipe:  BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds commit 590a6612d7d961e9258429e501619e0b7d7cbedf

Because the FFmpeg DLLs are linked dynamically and their file names are not
changed, a user may replace them with their own build of the same ABI
(avcodec-61 / avformat-61 / avutil-59 / swscale-8 / swresample-5).

The BtbN build statically links a number of external libraries into those DLLs.
Their licences travel with the binaries, not with this repository; the exact set
is printed by the same `-version` command.  Notable ones are libmp3lame, libopus,
libvorbis, libtheora, libvpx, libwebp, libass, libfreetype, libharfbuzz,
libfribidi, libaom, libdav1d, librav1e, libsvtav1, libopenh264, libzimg, libsoxr,
libsnappy and zlib (LGPL / MIT / BSD-style), plus gmp and libaribb24 (LGPL v3) and
libvmaf and libopencore-amr (Apache-2.0) — the last four are why
`--enable-version3` is required for this configuration.

libopenh264 (Cisco, BSD 2-Clause) is the H.264 *encoder* of this configuration,
`libx264` being disabled.  It is what generates the test fixture
`daw_gui/tests/fixtures/smoke_test.mp4` and the temporary clips that the video
tests encode at runtime, so that everything this repository produces comes out of
the same LGPL build it declares.

FFmpeg also contains three files taken from the Independent JPEG Group's libjpeg
(`libavcodec/jfdctfst.c`, `libavcodec/jfdctint_template.c`, `libavcodec/jrevdct.c`).
Their licence asks that, when only executables are distributed, the IJG be
credited in the accompanying documentation:

    This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

FFmpeg source code: https://ffmpeg.org/download.html
FFmpeg licensing:   https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html
LGPL v3 text:       https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html

**Mirror and Corresponding Source.**  BtbN keeps daily builds for about two
weeks, so the pinned URL will eventually stop resolving.  This project therefore
mirrors that exact zip in its own releases, under the tag
`vendor-ffmpeg-n7.1.5-16-g9a4bb2c579`.  Hosting the object code makes this
project a conveyor of it, so the same release also carries its Corresponding
Source, as GPL-3.0 section 6(d) requires (LGPL-3.0 incorporates the GPL's terms):

  * the FFmpeg source at commit 9a4bb2c579a16b0469759743d6917d9e8e3cb8c6,
  * the BtbN build recipe at commit 590a6612d7d961e9258429e501619e0b7d7cbedf --
    the "scripts to control those activities" of the GPL's definition, whose
    scripts.d/*.sh pin the revision of every statically linked library,
  * the sources of those statically linked libraries themselves, because
    BtbN links them into the DLLs (`--pkg-config-flags=--static`), which makes
    them part of the work rather than tools used to build it,
  * `BUILD_CONFIGURATION.txt` with the configure line read back from the shipped
    binary, as ffmpeg.org/legal.html asks for,
  * the GPL v3 text, because the zip ships only the LGPL v3 text and LGPL v3 is
    a set of additional permissions layered on the GPL v3.

`make ffmpeg-mirror` assembles all of that; `docs/ffmpeg_mirror.md` documents it.
The binary assets and the source assets are published and withdrawn together.

When a built copy of daw_01 is distributed, the LGPL v3 text must travel with the
FFmpeg DLLs.  `make fetch-ffmpeg` places it at `third_party/ffmpeg/LICENSE.txt`.

The file `daw_gui/ffmpeg/binding_ffmpeg_7.1.rs` in this repository is
rust-bindgen output generated from the FFmpeg public headers.  Those headers
carry "GNU Lesser General Public License ... version 2.1 ... or (at your option)
any later version", so the generated file is licensed **LGPL-2.1-or-later**, not
GPL.  See REUSE.toml.


